# The A2 root system, the roots of su(3), modeled as a REAL CONSTRUCTED set of roots with its symmetries. A root system is
# a finite set of vectors closed under negation and under the reflections in each root (the Weyl group). A2 has six roots:
# the simple roots a and b, their sum c = a + b, and the three negatives. The kernel proves the defining axioms on the
# constructed roots: negation is an involution (the set is closed under negation), the Weyl reflection in a is an
# involution that PERMUTES the six roots (closed under reflection), and the reflection commutes with negation. This is a
# root system as the structure itself, with computable negation and reflection, not a count of roots. A2 is the rank-two
# case; the same shape scales up through D4 (the 24-cell), F4, and E8.

# The six roots of A2: positives a, b, c = a+b, and their negatives.
form root
  case pa
  case pb
  case pc
  case na
  case nb
  case nc

# TEMPLATE: one entry of a single-valued map on roots, `from` sent to `to`. Replaces every `case .. / send back / make ..`
# block with one line per entry.
tree map-root
  take from
  take to

  hook fuse
    case {from}
      send back
        make {to}

# Negation: each root and its opposite. The root system is closed under this.
task negate
  take r, like root
  like root
  fork case, read r
    fuse map-root, pa, na
    fuse map-root, pb, nb
    fuse map-root, pc, nc
    fuse map-root, na, pa
    fuse map-root, nb, pb
    fuse map-root, nc, pc

# The WEYL REFLECTION in the root a: it negates a, and swaps b with c = a+b (since reflecting b across a adds a). The
# defining symmetry of the root system, a reflection that maps roots to roots.
task reflect-a
  take r, like root
  like root
  fork case, read r
    fuse map-root, pa, na
    fuse map-root, na, pa
    fuse map-root, pb, pc
    fuse map-root, pc, pb
    fuse map-root, nb, nc
    fuse map-root, nc, nb

# NEGATION IS AN INVOLUTION: negate (negate r) = r. The set of roots is closed under negation, each root paired with its
# opposite (the six roots are three lines, like the 24-cell's twelve).
rule negate-is-an-involution
  seat r, like root
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call negate
        call negate
          read r
      read r
  fold r

# THE REFLECTION IS AN INVOLUTION: reflect-a (reflect-a r) = r. Reflecting twice in the same root returns the original, the
# mark of a genuine reflection (a Weyl group generator, order two).
rule reflect-a-is-an-involution
  seat r, like root
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call reflect-a
        call reflect-a
          read r
      read r
  fold r

# THE REFLECTION COMMUTES WITH NEGATION: reflect-a (negate r) = negate (reflect-a r), for every root. The reflection
# respects the root-and-opposite pairing, a symmetry of the whole root system. With the involutions above, this shows the
# Weyl reflection is a genuine automorphism of the constructed root set.
rule reflection-commutes-with-negation
  seat r, like root
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call reflect-a
        call negate
          read r
      call negate
        call reflect-a
          read r
  fold r
